      { text: 'Benchmarking', cls: 'tag-cyan' },
      { text: 'Systems', cls: 'tag-amber' },
      { text: 'Interactive', cls: 'tag-green' },
    ],
    title: 'Your LLM Benchmark Is Lying to You',
    desc: 'At 1,000 QPS, single-process asyncio tools achieve only 14–44% of their target request rate and inject up to 58 seconds of fake latency — all due to Python\'s GIL. A Google paper models this with M/G/1 queueing theory, formalizes the NTPOT metric, and fixes it with a multi-process architecture that cuts artificial overhead to 0.63ms.',
